WebGPU: no timestamp queries in the browser

A timer pass writes only its beginning timestamp and leaves the end index undefined. Through the emdawnwebgpu port
that index reaches the browser as 0xffffffff, which Chrome rejects ("endOfPassWriteIndex is too large"), and the
rejection invalidates every command buffer of the frame: nothing is drawn.

diff --git a/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp b/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
index 3a4cf85..ee335aa 100644
--- a/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
@@ -6752,7 +6752,11 @@ WGPU_IMPORT
 	{
 		m_result.reset();
 
-		m_supported = isFeatureSupported(WGPUFeatureName_TimestampQuery);
+		// In the browser a timer pass writes only its beginning timestamp, and the end index it leaves undefined
+		// reaches the page as 0xffffffff, which invalidates every command buffer of the frame.
+		m_supported = !BX_ENABLED(BX_PLATFORM_EMSCRIPTEN)
+			&& isFeatureSupported(WGPUFeatureName_TimestampQuery)
+			;
 
 		if (!m_supported)
 		{
